WEBVTT

00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:01.660
Thank you.

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:40.470
But they're making...

00:01:59.250 --> 00:01:59.970
For the room with each...

00:02:00.090 --> 00:02:00.810
Jane's are hooping it up.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:01.480
Jane.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:03.240
Jane who?

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:04.120
The A.G.

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:04.700
When am I?

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:05.420
I've got it written down here.

00:02:05.800 --> 00:02:07.460
The Aero Girls of America.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:08.800
Miss Vi Benton's party.

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:10.220
I guess that's the name.

00:02:10.460 --> 00:02:11.400
You can't go in.

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:12.010
No.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:12.390
No.

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.640
I've been asked by Miss Benton, the hostess of the party, to guard the place.

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:18.620
See that no men get in there.

00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:19.950
Say, who are you, anyway?

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.880
My name happens to be Partington Chelmsford.

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:23.990
Partington Chelmsford?

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:26.140
Sir Horace Partington Chelmsford.

00:02:26.240 --> 00:02:26.740
Am I right?

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:27.080
Yes.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.900
Yes, say, the story is that you're, uh...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:36.310
up on Miss Benton. Is that set? Is what set? Engaged. She's not set. Well, I'll ask her

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:42.120
myself. From all accounts, she's a great girl. And this looks like a great party. Look here.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:47.100
Who are you nosing around at this time of night asking about things that don't concern

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.920
you? Who are you? What are you? I'm just a poor little tired reporter from the morning

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.700
echo. And I want to get this story and go home and go to bed.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:12.820
shake our little hips to England.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:16.400
Da, da, da, da, da, da, da, da, da.

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:17.340
Now seriously, girls,

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:21.260
we're going to get into a lot of awfully good European competition.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:24.210
But when the international trophy is presented,

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:25.900
who are the girls going to win it?

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:26.560
That's right.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:36.730
about your behavior oh sorry oh i'm the sap that's sponsoring this boat ride and i want you high

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:46.300
flyers to remember to keep your tanks clean your landing gears on the ground and don't go into any

00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:12.580
and my boss. And I know there's a very good reason why he hasn't turned up.

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:16.680
However, we're going right on with the meeting. We are honored tonight

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:20.880
with the presence of Mr. Timothy Grovener, President of the National

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:23.980
Seaboard Bank. Mr. Grovener, thank you, sir.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:29.770
It is to be regretted that the guest of honor is late.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:33.190
For the purpose of this dinner, as I understand it,

00:04:33.560 --> 00:04:35.500
was a gesture made by you gentlemen

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:38.460
as a token of esteem to a young man

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:42.040
who has been somewhat aptly termed in the last year

00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:44.420
a modern financial wizard.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.340
Say, if you don't think that cop situation is a wow,

00:04:57.480 --> 00:04:58.320
then I'm an Egyptian.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:04:59.960
Ha! We've been fighting for the last...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.540
two hours to stabilize the cotton market.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:02.920
Sorry you're not aboard, baby.

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:05.580
Larry, Mr. Grosvenor's making a speech.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:07.660
Oh, hello, Mr. Grosvenor. How are you? Glad to see you.

00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:08.560
Go right ahead. Go on.

00:05:08.860 --> 00:05:11.800
In view of the fact that this dinner was given in your honor, Mr. Day,

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:15.000
I should have thought some sort of an apology might have been forthcoming.

00:05:15.140 --> 00:05:16.980
Well, it's all right. Don't apologize. Go right ahead.

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:18.360
Go mind me. Go on, Mr. Grosvenor.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:20.020
Please go right on. Please go right on, Mr. Grosvenor.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:20.640
Don't mind, Larry.

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.160
But even now, Mr. Day's attention is elsewhere.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:25.080
Order, Larry. Order, please.

00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:25.400
Order.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:26.980
Sure, I'll order. I've had my dinner.

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:28.560
Waiter, waiter. Go on, Mr. Grosvenor.

00:05:28.560 --> 00:05:29.980
What are you fellas eating here?

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.800
No wonder you're losing your waistline.

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:33.480
Here, give this to a bellboy and let him eat it for me.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:35.280
Bring me some cornflakes and milk. Warm.

00:05:35.780 --> 00:05:36.840
That's right. Go on, Mr. Grover.

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:39.120
Please continue, would you, Mr. Grover? Please.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:44.420
To resume, in the music of the word,

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:47.640
America can be heard the distant drums of Gettysburg.

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:49.920
Uh, Mr. Day, London on the telephone, sir.

00:05:50.020 --> 00:05:51.980
London. All right, fine. Excuse me, Mr. Grover.

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:54.060
Go on, Mr. Grover. I respect this call all afternoon.

00:05:54.440 --> 00:05:56.180
All right. I'm very proud of you, Mr. Grover,

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:57.160
but please don't mind laughing.

00:05:57.680 --> 00:05:58.660
Come on, London!

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:01.560
That check certified?

00:06:02.390 --> 00:06:02.770
Captain?

00:06:04.070 --> 00:06:04.470
Receited?

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:06.110
Ah, that's fine.

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:06.770
Ha, ha.

00:06:07.070 --> 00:06:08.090
How many bales?

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:09.680
A million bales.

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:11.080
What do you know about that?

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:11.640
Fine.

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:12.120
Why?

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:13.500
What do you know about that?

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:15.980
Those Egyptians had a million bales of cotton

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:17.320
to dump on a market and break it,

00:06:17.380 --> 00:06:18.840
but we feed them to it and bought control.

00:06:19.220 --> 00:06:20.760
Watch cotton open in the morning.

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:21.700
Ha, ha.

00:06:22.040 --> 00:06:23.640
Go ahead, Miss Irwin.

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:25.680
Gentlemen, now that you wish that I continue.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:26.720
Oh, yes, indeed.

00:06:26.940 --> 00:06:27.120
Please.

00:06:27.440 --> 00:06:28.280
Yes, go on.

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:29.970
As I said before,

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:31.690
All Americans.

00:06:32.210 --> 00:06:40.570
This, Mr. Day, is an American made out of the kind of grit that gave us our Gary's, our Schwab's, our Henry Ford's.

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:41.750
And our Kellogg's.

00:06:43.270 --> 00:06:43.670
Order.

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:45.130
Hang on, man.

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:47.790
Keep going my way, Preston.

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:48.710
I'm good.

00:06:48.910 --> 00:06:49.290
I'm sorry.

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:51.250
Hey, Larry, apologize to him.

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:52.430
Please, hurt his feelings.

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:53.170
Go on and apologize.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:54.770
I wouldn't hurt his feelings for any of the work.

00:06:55.830 --> 00:06:57.270
Mr. Carlin, just a moment.

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:57.890
Just a moment.

00:06:58.190 --> 00:06:59.650
You know, your speech was fine.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.920
Boy, she was great.

00:07:01.240 --> 00:07:02.900
I like that thing about Americans.

00:07:03.120 --> 00:07:04.140
You're not upset, are you?

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:04.980
Upset?

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:05.520
Yes.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:08.220
You know, I had one of those days, you know, cotton situations.

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:09.620
Yes, I see, I see.

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:12.060
You know, I wouldn't intentionally be rude for anything in the world.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:12.720
I see.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:17.900
One must not impede this explosive urge, this new, young America.

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:19.460
Well, you do understand, don't you?

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:19.840
Certainly.

00:07:19.980 --> 00:07:20.560
That's fine.

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:21.080
Okay?

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:22.280
Good night.

00:07:22.540 --> 00:07:23.060
Good night?

00:07:23.340 --> 00:07:27.060
Really, you know, Larry's happy as a king.

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:04.340
Yes, I know. This is a party, isn't it?

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:05.700
Say, has Vi gone yet?

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:07.260
No, she's here. Is this your crowd?

00:08:07.420 --> 00:08:08.240
I'd like to dance.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.210
Yes, darling, but that's pretty old.

00:08:10.410 --> 00:08:11.980
Never mind them men.

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:14.650
Hello, darling.

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:14.990
Secret?

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:15.890
Men, though.

00:08:16.880 --> 00:08:17.480
Men, will you?

00:08:17.680 --> 00:08:18.860
What do you mean men?

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:23.950
That man and the brave students.

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:25.910
That's Larry Day.

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:28.390
That happens to be my boss.

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:29.960
No, I don't know.

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:31.440
It's early.

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:33.080
Yeah, well, it's early for you, but late for me.

00:08:33.160 --> 00:08:33.500
Oh, come on.

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:35.710
It's a big day tomorrow.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:36.410
You can't have boom.

00:08:36.630 --> 00:08:37.210
Good night, Larry.

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:38.250
Good night.

00:08:38.710 --> 00:08:42.030
Remember, we're on the verge of a big boom, and tomorrow morning, I'm shooting the work.

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:42.970
Do you think that's a good idea?

00:08:43.070 --> 00:08:43.810
It's the only idea.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:44.490
You take it from me.

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:45.690
He looks all right.

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:46.800
He is.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:49.200
I'd like to meet him.

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:51.030
I will if I can.

00:08:51.350 --> 00:08:52.640
What do you will if you can?

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:54.160
I mean, I'll try.

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:55.760
You'll try.

00:09:00.570 --> 00:09:01.410
Just a moment, please.

00:09:01.710 --> 00:09:03.610
Hey, Larry, I want you to meet a very, very beautiful girl.

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:04.930
Well, you're a crazy man.

00:09:05.010 --> 00:09:06.010
I'm going home to go to bed.

00:09:06.150 --> 00:09:07.150
No, really, I mean it.

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:07.890
Well, I mean it, too.

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:08.750
I've got to get my sleep.

00:09:09.110 --> 00:09:10.540
But I ought to say hello to her.

00:09:10.540 --> 00:09:15.820
Well, you say hello if you saw the dirty day.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:18.280
Well, I won't see her because I can't stay.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:20.400
Well, look, she's standing right over there.

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:20.980
Would you take a look?

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:22.760
No, I won't, because I've got to go get my sleep.

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:23.740
You better get to her sleep, too.

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:24.740
I'll see you bright night in the morning.

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:38.380
Well, there you are. That's the kind of a guy he is.

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:41.570
No, seriously, Vi, I don't believe there's a girl in this town who can get him.

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:44.010
Well, of course, there's always a river.

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:49.350
Oh, yes, just like a dynamo.

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:52.210
Pity I'm sailing tomorrow night on La Merite.

00:09:52.470 --> 00:09:54.430
But a lot can be done in the morning, Vi.

00:09:54.650 --> 00:09:56.420
Good afternoon for that matter.

00:09:59.250 --> 00:09:59.610
See you, thanks.

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:02.090
Well, you never could see him in the daytime.

00:10:02.670 --> 00:10:04.370
I work for him and even I can't.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:06.370
No? Well, it might be fun to try.

00:10:07.450 --> 00:10:08.850
What are you laughing at?

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:11.170
Oh, by betting that Larry did.

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:13.170
Dynamite. Explosion?

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:15.290
You couldn't do it.

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:17.100
Well, I haven't got much time, but

00:10:17.100 --> 00:10:18.500
give me odds and I'll bet you.

00:10:18.940 --> 00:10:21.180
On deck, bet you.

00:10:21.380 --> 00:10:24.070
Oh, Horace.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:29.660
It's very nice.

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:38.780
I'm afraid I'm going to be awfully busy in the morning.

00:10:38.900 --> 00:10:39.620
Good night, Admiral.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:41.460
Busy with Larry's day.

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:46.040
Does father come in yet?

00:10:46.510 --> 00:10:46.970
No, miss.

00:10:57.290 --> 00:10:59.650
After all, you know, one little kiss.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.180
It is a very small matter.

00:11:01.440 --> 00:11:02.300
Oh, don't be silly.

00:11:03.060 --> 00:11:07.550
Di, you're the coldest creature, but I adore you.

00:11:08.030 --> 00:11:08.250
Thanks.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:10.840
I console myself with the thought

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:13.720
that underneath your somewhat frigid exterior,

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:16.330
there thumps a jolly little huff,

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:20.360
going bumpity-bump, bumpity-bump, beating away from me.

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:23.300
But I'm beating away from you, old darling,

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:24.920
because I'm going after bed.

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:26.340
Excellent place, Dad.

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:27.830
Hello, Paula's girl.

00:11:28.010 --> 00:11:28.650
Good evening, sir.

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:33.240
I thought I told them not to lock that door.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:35.540
I thought you said my father wasn't in.

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:41.460
He's just come in, miss, through the service and through school, my darling.

00:11:41.870 --> 00:11:42.930
Hello, my darling.

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:44.120
Where have you been?

00:11:45.080 --> 00:11:46.380
I've been playing bridge.

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:47.940
Where?

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:50.840
Downstairs, in the apartment.

00:11:52.700 --> 00:11:53.540
Contract bridge?

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:55.940
Oh, speaking of contract, why?

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:59.200
Is your engagement to this young man to be kept secret?

00:12:00.380 --> 00:12:01.180
Oh, I don't know.

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:05.250
In my considered opinion, Governor, long engagements are fatal.

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:07.420
Well, good night, Harrod.

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:09.380
Oh, good night, darling.

00:12:11.630 --> 00:12:12.590
Good night, my child.

00:12:13.470 --> 00:12:13.870
Good night.

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:23.580
I say, do you realize that I've been secretly engaged to your fair daughter for months,

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:26.580
both of us madly in love with each other and all that sort of thing,

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:28.560
and I haven't been kissed once?

00:12:29.150 --> 00:12:29.970
We've soon fixed...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:30.260
What's that?

00:12:32.840 --> 00:12:33.560
What for country?

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:45.810
Man.

00:12:49.850 --> 00:12:50.570
Sure I did.

00:12:51.690 --> 00:12:53.070
Have him paged and call me.

00:12:54.150 --> 00:12:54.710
Yes, I'll wait.

00:13:12.440 --> 00:13:12.780
What is it?

00:13:12.940 --> 00:13:14.100
Oh, I've just seen her, sir.

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:14.420
Who?

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:15.840
Oh, a veritable Juliet.

00:13:20.870 --> 00:13:24.310
You get a big kick out of that sort of thing, don't you?

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:24.800
Peepy.

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:28.110
Well, I find it's a very instructive study, sir.

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:29.320
Yes, sir.

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:32.150
Just as you obtain results by watching the market,

00:13:32.350 --> 00:13:35.350
so I learn the different methods of making love by observation.

00:13:36.420 --> 00:13:41.290
And I find these observations are much more effective than certain books.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:45.700
Aren't you a little bit afraid that you're liable to go boom?

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:50.840
Oh, may I suggest, sir, that you'll come to it too?

00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:54.340
What do you mean that I'll go boom?

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:59.980
Oh, my dear sir, why, anyone worth saying than yourself would be very hard to find.

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:03.700
But all the great ones of the world fell at one time or another, sir.

00:14:04.100 --> 00:14:04.800
You take Napoleon.

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:07.430
Napoleon studied to be a great soldier.

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:09.380
And he was a very great general.

00:14:09.640 --> 00:14:11.920
And then little Josephine came tripling into his life.

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:14.270
And a very great general went poof.

00:14:17.610 --> 00:14:19.920
So you think I'm liable to go poof?

00:14:21.680 --> 00:14:26.960
Well, there's a vast difference, sir, between the art of making money and the art of making a lady.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.170
Well, there's plenty of time, Roger.

00:14:36.480 --> 00:14:37.960
You shouldn't have been a valet, huh?

00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:40.100
Hurry up that car, will you?

00:14:41.670 --> 00:14:42.450
Make a lady.

00:14:44.460 --> 00:14:44.980
What's this?

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:46.230
Napoleon, sir.

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:46.910
Napoleon?

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:47.590
At Elba.

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:50.850
A great man, sir, but lonely.

00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:52.430
Well, maybe you're right, Roger.

00:14:52.710 --> 00:14:53.630
There's plenty of time for that.

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:55.190
When the time comes, I'll be there.

00:14:55.250 --> 00:14:55.850
You know me, Roger.

00:14:56.150 --> 00:14:57.350
Anything I go after, I get.

00:14:58.560 --> 00:14:58.920
Hello.

00:14:59.460 --> 00:14:59.960
Oh, hello, friend.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:03.360
Now listen, 8.30 in the morning, I want you to go to my vault and get all my securities.

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:05.680
Yeah, Bankers Trust, Mellon's Trust, and Guaranty Trust.

00:15:05.860 --> 00:15:06.200
That's right.

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:07.170
Right?

00:15:08.110 --> 00:15:09.410
