00:35:08.860 --> 00:35:10.460
There's a Polish woman in the second cabin.

00:35:10.710 --> 00:35:11.250
A blonde.

00:35:11.730 --> 00:35:12.630
I may be two hours.

00:35:13.040 --> 00:35:13.780
I can't tell.

00:35:13.980 --> 00:35:14.460
Who knows?

00:35:16.670 --> 00:35:18.090
Well, hasta mañana.

00:35:19.000 --> 00:35:19.260
Yes?

00:35:19.880 --> 00:35:21.380
You do, and you'll attend to it yourself.

00:35:24.150 --> 00:35:24.910
Ha, ha, ha.

00:35:25.380 --> 00:35:25.600
Ha!

00:35:27.040 --> 00:35:28.100
Oh, ahem.

00:35:32.590 --> 00:35:35.840
Vivian, ever since I've been on this boat.

00:35:36.720 --> 00:35:50.360
Sorry, Dave, sorry.

00:35:53.310 --> 00:35:54.710
Ah, nice little cabin you have here.

00:36:03.870 --> 00:36:05.230
Well, what can I do for you?

00:36:06.420 --> 00:36:08.540
Dave, I don't know whether you happen to be aware

00:36:08.540 --> 00:36:10.760
that I'm the fiance to Miss Benton.

00:36:12.880 --> 00:36:13.100
What?

00:36:14.200 --> 00:36:15.260
We're engaged to be married.

00:36:17.000 --> 00:36:20.110
Who? You? Why?

00:36:20.370 --> 00:36:21.130
Miss Benton.

00:36:23.120 --> 00:36:23.480
No.

00:36:24.000 --> 00:36:24.420
Oh, yes.

00:36:24.630 --> 00:36:25.210
Oh, you're kidding.

00:36:25.450 --> 00:36:26.130
On the contrary.

00:36:27.040 --> 00:36:29.970
However, in view of the fact that you were in ignorance of this,

00:36:30.000 --> 00:36:33.920
I'm prepared to overlook what might have been consummate impertinent on your part

00:36:33.920 --> 00:36:36.760
in asking her here alone for a cocktail.

00:36:37.420 --> 00:36:38.520
You mean that she's not coming?

00:36:38.680 --> 00:36:40.650
Of course she's not coming. I've forbidden her.

00:36:43.160 --> 00:36:46.920
Sorry to be the bearer of such old tidings, but there you are.

00:36:47.230 --> 00:36:52.750
So you're not coming. It's all joke.

00:36:55.910 --> 00:36:56.950
What did you say, Danny?

00:36:58.940 --> 00:36:59.740
Oh, have a drink.

00:37:00.160 --> 00:37:00.620
A drink?

00:37:00.800 --> 00:37:01.400
I do, yes.

00:37:01.540 --> 00:37:02.220
Well, you better go.

00:37:02.550 --> 00:37:03.250
Thanks very much.

00:37:04.360 --> 00:37:05.540
Hello, cocktails, eh?

00:37:06.100 --> 00:37:07.780
I save quite a few ingredients, too.

00:37:10.970 --> 00:37:11.670
Well, cheerio.

00:37:12.390 --> 00:37:15.130
Happiness, prosperity, love one another's always.

00:37:28.960 --> 00:37:29.640
Not coming.

00:37:30.250 --> 00:37:30.590
What?

00:37:33.960 --> 00:37:35.020
You said she's not coming.

00:37:35.160 --> 00:37:36.420
I told you she wasn't coming.

00:37:39.180 --> 00:37:40.220
And look here, Dave.

00:37:41.090 --> 00:37:45.050
I'm slow to anger, but once roused, I'm something to cope with.

00:37:48.920 --> 00:37:58.220
And I'm quite prepared to defend my rights with a sock on the nose, a punch on the jaw, a kick in the back.

00:38:00.160 --> 00:38:01.280
Ha, ha, ha, ha, ha.

00:38:30.570 --> 00:38:34.250
The first drink of my life to the first love of my life.

00:39:00.920 --> 00:39:03.880
To your ladyship, long life, and happiness.

00:39:05.310 --> 00:39:07.340
Oh, you wouldn't be happy with him.

00:39:15.890 --> 00:39:18.150
No matter what happens, I'll always drink to you.

00:39:18.310 --> 00:39:22.600
Drink, drink, drink to the world!

00:39:33.230 --> 00:39:33.750
Wow.

00:40:00.250 --> 00:40:02.400
Look here, what is this?

00:40:08.900 --> 00:40:09.860
Steady, steady.

00:40:11.140 --> 00:40:16.340
Look here, I've stopped.

00:40:16.740 --> 00:40:18.240
I've positively stopped now.

00:40:18.800 --> 00:40:20.180
Oh, my goodness, sir.

00:40:22.050 --> 00:40:23.630
Right there, I'm glad you came.

00:40:24.040 --> 00:40:24.860
Is Mr. Day here?

00:40:25.160 --> 00:40:26.070
Is he here?

00:40:27.940 --> 00:40:29.620
Look out, look out.

00:40:35.280 --> 00:40:37.160
To me! Help!

00:40:37.520 --> 00:40:38.320
You, cabin boy!

00:40:38.400 --> 00:40:38.800
To me!

00:40:39.060 --> 00:40:40.160
Come on!

00:40:40.280 --> 00:40:40.540
Come on!

00:40:40.680 --> 00:40:41.820
To me!

00:40:42.200 --> 00:40:43.550
Go away!

00:40:43.750 --> 00:40:44.110
Come on!

00:40:44.830 --> 00:40:45.330
Yes!

00:41:05.080 --> 00:41:05.600
That's a country!

00:41:35.020 --> 00:41:36.560
Are you hurt, sir?

00:41:37.370 --> 00:41:37.630
No.

00:41:38.250 --> 00:41:39.150
A doctor, perhaps?

00:41:39.350 --> 00:41:39.550
No.

00:41:40.010 --> 00:41:41.250
Well, sir, I'll draw you a cold bath.

00:41:41.370 --> 00:41:42.510
You'll be all right in just a moment, sir.

00:41:42.550 --> 00:41:44.170
The effect goes just as quickly as it comes.

00:41:52.560 --> 00:41:53.480
Miss Benton, sir.

00:41:53.940 --> 00:41:55.240
No, she's not coming.

00:41:55.580 --> 00:41:57.080
Well, that's coming.

00:41:59.140 --> 00:41:59.900
I thought he didn't drink.

00:42:00.190 --> 00:42:02.070
He doesn't. He thought you weren't coming.

00:42:02.370 --> 00:42:08.940
Well, then.

00:42:31.690 --> 00:42:38.160
Congratulations. I wish you every happiness in the world.

00:42:48.100 --> 00:42:54.400
And a very great general went poof.

00:43:00.990 --> 00:43:01.710
Excuse me.

00:43:38.120 --> 00:43:38.400
Thank you.

00:44:00.800 --> 00:44:02.140
Oh, that's so.

00:44:03.720 --> 00:44:04.700
Oh, that's so.

00:44:05.700 --> 00:44:06.640
Oh, pardon me.

00:44:06.940 --> 00:44:07.160
Oh, thank you.

00:44:08.730 --> 00:44:10.490
Oh, thank you.

00:44:10.870 --> 00:44:11.290
Oh, thank you.

00:44:11.450 --> 00:44:16.970
Oh, for goodness sake.

00:44:17.110 --> 00:44:17.910
What's wrong about it?

00:44:21.800 --> 00:44:22.820
Oh, yes.

00:45:31.180 --> 00:45:34.050
Avenue's learning how to deploy

00:45:35.800 --> 00:45:36.920
And who does it now?

00:45:39.410 --> 00:45:43.940
Folks, that means now

00:45:47.580 --> 00:45:50.470
But as well, they come

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:07.840
I just don't make up

00:47:30.250 --> 00:47:38.660
I want to tell those for comfort.

00:47:43.340 --> 00:47:47.920
Something for today.

00:47:48.300 --> 00:47:48.500
What?

00:47:48.780 --> 00:47:50.200
Would you care for something for today?

00:47:50.560 --> 00:47:53.280
Very, very, very, very much.

00:48:30.410 --> 00:48:44.420
I still am!

00:48:45.100 --> 00:48:46.160
Hey, what did you...

00:48:47.460 --> 00:48:47.840
Yes!

00:48:49.080 --> 00:48:50.180
What did you put in them?

00:48:50.460 --> 00:48:50.680
Yes!

00:48:55.380 --> 00:48:55.700
No!

00:48:58.950 --> 00:48:59.290
Yes!

00:49:06.330 --> 00:49:12.350
Come and sing again.

00:49:13.010 --> 00:49:13.850
Oh, do, please.

00:49:38.350 --> 00:49:38.830
Friday night.

00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:48.200
getting away from the crowd we land in four hours and I may never see you again

00:50:48.200 --> 00:50:55.450
I'm going back to New York I suppose I shouldn't say to this to you after what

00:50:55.450 --> 00:50:59.960
I heard this afternoon but there was a reason why

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:01.420
I left New York at a moment's notice.

00:51:01.580 --> 00:51:03.880
And there was a reason why I hadn't taken my eyes off you.

00:51:04.100 --> 00:51:10.360
There was a reason why I gave up everything I thought was best in the world.

00:51:11.640 --> 00:51:18.280
That reason was that I found myself for the first time in my life in love,

00:51:20.280 --> 00:51:22.700
madly, desperately in love.

00:51:27.470 --> 00:51:28.650
I suppose I shouldn't say this.

00:51:29.160 --> 00:51:29.800
It was forgiving.

00:51:32.940 --> 00:51:34.020
But I had to tell you.

00:51:35.030 --> 00:51:36.570
Oh, Larry, you're sweet.

00:51:37.280 --> 00:51:38.800
I like you awfully.

00:51:40.220 --> 00:51:40.620
Do you?

00:51:42.650 --> 00:51:43.690
Well, let me tell you something.

00:51:51.690 --> 00:51:55.700
Never since I was a kid of ten and knelt to my mother

00:51:56.780 --> 00:51:58.920
have I felt like kneeling to anyone.

00:52:02.780 --> 00:52:06.310
But you are my idol, and I worship you.

00:52:07.650 --> 00:52:11.440
There'll never be anyone else but you, ever.

00:52:34.120 --> 00:52:35.380
Are you laughing at me?

00:52:36.900 --> 00:52:37.320
No.

00:52:38.960 --> 00:52:40.400
Why, you're laughing at me.

00:52:40.650 --> 00:52:41.170
I'm not.

00:52:41.740 --> 00:52:42.480
Don't lie.

00:52:44.020 --> 00:52:44.920
I'm not lying.

00:52:45.100 --> 00:52:45.900
You are lying.

00:52:46.000 --> 00:52:46.780
You're laughing at me.

00:52:46.840 --> 00:52:48.900
That's a low, rotten, despicable trick.

00:52:52.070 --> 00:52:52.590
Dare you.

00:52:52.770 --> 00:52:53.970
Oh, you're laughing at me.

00:52:54.510 --> 00:52:55.890
Yes, I'm laughing at you.

00:52:56.070 --> 00:52:56.350
Hmm.

00:52:56.550 --> 00:52:57.350
You fool.

00:52:58.150 --> 00:52:59.090
Oh, there you are, Vivian.

00:52:59.460 --> 00:52:59.960
Yes, you're...

00:53:00.400 --> 00:53:01.960
I've been looking for you all over the boat.

00:53:02.100 --> 00:53:02.780
Something everywhere.

00:53:03.040 --> 00:53:04.840
In the corridors, in the card room, and everywhere.

00:53:06.240 --> 00:53:14.450
If I had known you were going to bring an audience,

00:53:15.780 --> 00:53:16.900
I would have put on a better show.

00:53:18.770 --> 00:53:19.150
Good night.

00:53:19.740 --> 00:53:21.000
You know that fellow's gone potty.

00:53:21.080 --> 00:53:22.020
What's he talking about?

00:53:24.090 --> 00:53:26.290
Oh, I'm sorry, Vi. The canvas broke.

00:53:26.530 --> 00:53:27.110
Get out of here!

00:53:28.100 --> 00:53:29.300
Come along, Vi. Let's dance.

00:53:30.280 --> 00:53:31.780
Goodbye, please. Come on.

00:53:31.900 --> 00:53:33.080
Leave me alone, will you?

00:53:33.280 --> 00:53:34.100
Oh, all right.

00:53:49.220 --> 00:53:50.620
I've been looking all over for you, Mr. Day.

00:53:50.880 --> 00:53:51.220
Where is it?

00:53:51.320 --> 00:53:52.440
New York. It's on the telephone.

00:53:52.740 --> 00:53:53.000
Where?

00:53:53.140 --> 00:53:54.040
It's in the Marconi room.

00:53:54.660 --> 00:53:55.400
Where's the Marconi room?

00:53:55.440 --> 00:53:58.140
Why, uh, this way, sir.

00:54:04.960 --> 00:54:05.880
Mr. Day is here.

00:54:08.360 --> 00:54:08.800
Mr. Day.

00:54:09.100 --> 00:54:09.720
Where's that telephone?

00:54:10.160 --> 00:54:10.760
Right there, sir.

00:54:14.370 --> 00:54:16.590
I'm sorry, Larry, but I'm broke, too.

00:54:16.930 --> 00:54:19.960
Dylan, broke, too.

00:54:23.040 --> 00:54:23.680
Where's that telephone?

00:54:24.680 --> 00:54:25.120
Right here, sir.

00:54:37.260 --> 00:54:47.360
that's all hello hello Carrington well what's it all about stop crying go on

00:54:47.360 --> 00:54:58.200
tell me now you saw Grafton Sutherland they wouldn't carry

00:55:01.500 --> 00:55:03.060
Yes, I just had a cable from Dillon.

00:55:03.300 --> 00:55:04.200
He said he's broke.

00:55:07.480 --> 00:55:09.540
Well, I'm in good company.

00:55:11.750 --> 00:55:13.470
What about those other securities in my vault?

00:55:13.630 --> 00:55:14.190
My insurance.

00:55:15.970 --> 00:55:16.990
Oh, yeah, I remember, I remember.

00:55:17.910 --> 00:55:18.870
In my power of attorney.

00:55:19.860 --> 00:55:20.080
Right.

00:55:22.200 --> 00:55:24.840
Well, that means I'm wiped out, and you don't mean maybe.

00:55:25.540 --> 00:55:25.940
Who?

00:55:30.700 --> 00:55:31.280
Grovener?

00:55:32.950 --> 00:55:33.550
Shot himself.

00:55:38.840 --> 00:55:39.960
No, I haven't seen a paper.

00:55:41.060 --> 00:55:42.040
No, I haven't read anything.

00:55:44.340 --> 00:55:45.960
What is steel closer?

00:55:48.080 --> 00:55:52.260
Oh, we still have the office furniture.

00:55:55.780 --> 00:55:57.540
Call you tomorrow from Southampton.

00:56:00.030 --> 00:56:00.610
Oh, I'm all right.

00:56:01.360 --> 00:56:01.700
Fine.

00:56:04.320 --> 00:56:05.200
Now stick to the ship.

00:57:37.540 --> 00:57:38.740
All right.

00:58:02.460 --> 00:58:14.690
Oh, why?

00:58:15.240 --> 00:58:16.460
Morris is looking for you.

00:58:16.640 --> 00:58:20.150
He wants you to wave to Lady Partington Chelmsford and her daughter.

00:58:20.440 --> 00:58:22.700
Oh, there you are, sir. I've been looking everywhere for you.

00:58:22.940 --> 00:58:24.680
Here's the Mater and Phyllis and Florence,

00:58:24.860 --> 00:58:26.000
and they're waiting to wait you.

00:58:26.080 --> 00:58:27.900
You must wait for them, too.

00:58:34.960 --> 00:58:35.740
They're just here.

00:58:37.960 --> 00:58:39.020
Hello, hello, hello.

00:58:40.740 --> 00:58:42.020
There they are, look, there they are.

00:58:42.140 --> 00:58:43.740
Here she is, here she is.

00:58:45.660 --> 00:58:46.640
Wave, wave.

00:58:47.240 --> 00:58:49.880
Wave back, wave back.

00:58:50.590 --> 00:58:51.690
That's right, that's right.

00:58:52.010 --> 00:58:54.350
I say, how old Poggy and Noggle?

00:58:54.660 --> 00:58:55.360
Where are they?

00:58:56.360 --> 00:58:57.760
Oh, I say, look by my dog.

00:58:58.040 --> 00:58:59.520
Poggy and Noggle.

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:03.320
I think they can smell me even from here.

00:59:03.860 --> 00:59:05.020
Bless their little heart.

00:59:05.360 --> 00:59:06.180
Lie down.

00:59:06.760 --> 00:59:07.660
Be dead.

00:59:07.860 --> 00:59:08.000
Dead.

00:59:08.780 --> 00:59:09.500
That's right.

00:59:09.720 --> 00:59:11.020
Look, he's gone.

00:59:16.700 --> 00:59:17.640
He's dead.

00:59:17.880 --> 00:59:29.690
Oh, good morning, Miss Benson.

00:59:30.220 --> 00:59:32.320
Where is he? I've searched all over the boat for him.

00:59:32.420 --> 00:59:33.480
Why, he's on deck A.

00:59:34.060 --> 00:59:35.130
Oh, oh yes.

00:59:35.330 --> 00:59:36.730
Yes, the boat deck, Ms. Benson.

00:59:37.600 --> 00:59:40.180
Thank you, Roger. I, I just wanted to say goodbye.

00:59:40.500 --> 00:59:40.780
Yes.

00:59:58.570 --> 00:59:59.970
Not land.

01:00:00.700 --> 01:00:01.080
No.

01:00:02.050 --> 01:00:03.560
I've been looking for you.

01:00:03.790 --> 01:00:04.170
Have you?

01:00:04.820 --> 01:00:06.790
Just wanted to say goodbye.

01:00:07.790 --> 01:00:09.270
Goodbye. It's been great fun.

01:00:10.350 --> 01:00:11.070
Beautiful fun.

01:00:11.520 --> 01:00:12.240
Beautiful fun.

01:00:12.880 --> 01:00:16.260
I wanted you to know that I didn't know those kids were there.

01:00:17.020 --> 01:00:17.760
What kids? Where?

01:00:18.610 --> 01:00:19.130
In the boat.

01:00:21.190 --> 01:00:22.030
I'm sure you did.

01:00:22.710 --> 01:00:24.150
You were very unkind.

01:00:24.720 --> 01:00:25.960
Was I? Well, I'm sorry.

01:00:26.600 --> 01:00:28.820
And I want you to know that you hurt my wrist.

01:00:29.190 --> 01:00:29.470
Look.

01:00:31.720 --> 01:00:34.880
So soft, huh?

01:00:35.710 --> 01:00:36.250
Still cross?

01:00:36.840 --> 01:00:37.100
Cross?

01:00:37.820 --> 01:00:38.740
Why not cross?

01:00:39.160 --> 01:00:42.710
Well, then, you know that I wasn't laughing at you.

01:00:42.880 --> 01:00:43.740
Oh, I'm sure you were.

01:00:44.020 --> 01:00:49.960
Don't you think that there's something rather sad about the end of the sea voyage?

01:00:50.320 --> 01:00:51.600
Yes, there is.

01:00:52.340 --> 01:00:53.810
Yes, there is.

01:00:54.770 --> 01:00:58.490
You know, this whole business has been sort of a hysterical thing.

01:00:58.650 --> 01:00:58.830
I...

01:00:59.200 --> 01:00:59.860
I...

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:05.280
came aboard the boat, and sort of reaching for the moon, and, well, I'm sorry about

01:01:05.280 --> 01:01:19.000
everything. Oh, don't be. It's been beautiful fun. Beautiful fun. Goodbye. Goodbye.

01:01:30.960 --> 01:01:32.340
Under the stairs, to your left.

01:01:32.600 --> 01:01:35.700
I would like everything left in the cabin until you hear definitely from me.

01:01:35.900 --> 01:01:36.180
I will.

01:01:36.420 --> 01:01:36.540
Thanks.

01:01:39.760 --> 01:01:40.580
Goodbye, Roger.

01:01:41.340 --> 01:01:41.860
You saw him?

01:01:42.470 --> 01:01:42.770
Yes.

01:01:43.090 --> 01:01:43.610
He told you?

01:01:44.440 --> 01:01:44.840
Yes.

01:01:46.180 --> 01:01:46.880
What do you mean?

01:01:47.000 --> 01:01:47.760
Tell me what?

01:01:48.530 --> 01:01:50.090
Well, you see, Miss Benton.

01:01:54.230 --> 01:01:58.990
And more than that, I believe there are tremendous obligations.

01:02:02.240 --> 01:02:04.710
So that's why he...

01:02:06.140 --> 01:02:07.590
Oh, I see.

01:02:10.960 --> 01:02:12.260
I'm going to him, Roger.

01:02:12.620 --> 01:02:13.440
Yes, Mrs. Smith.

01:02:36.560 --> 01:02:37.780
I want to tell you something.

01:02:40.500 --> 01:02:48.840
I just saw, Roger, last night you said that you'd never knelt to anyone but your mother.

01:02:48.860 --> 01:02:51.500
And I believed you.

01:02:53.540 --> 01:02:59.510
And I want you to believe me when I say that I've never been happy until...

01:03:01.760 --> 01:03:08.340
Well, I'm going to tell you something that I would have sworn I never would have told any man.

01:03:08.460 --> 01:03:14.060
I love you, Larry.

01:03:16.390 --> 01:03:16.870
You do?

01:03:20.270 --> 01:03:24.480
Yes, but it's out of the question.

01:03:25.560 --> 01:03:26.400
I'm broke.

01:03:28.560 --> 01:03:29.180
Why, you?

01:03:30.060 --> 01:03:32.920
Well, of course, you're, you're you.

01:03:33.720 --> 01:03:34.120
Me.

01:03:35.720 --> 01:03:36.700
You're worth millions.

01:03:37.000 --> 01:03:39.960
Oh, that doesn't make any difference.

01:03:40.280 --> 01:03:43.160
Oh, what kind of a man do you think I'd be?

01:03:44.560 --> 01:03:45.540
You're Larry Day.

01:03:46.140 --> 01:03:47.860
That's the kind of a man you are.

01:03:48.250 --> 01:03:50.580
Why, you couldn't be broke.

01:03:52.200 --> 01:03:53.700
I've known big men all my life.

01:03:54.310 --> 01:03:56.510
You can make this defortune sack.

01:03:57.340 --> 01:03:59.340
Why, do you think I love you the way I do it?

01:04:00.000 --> 01:04:04.120
If you weren't you, you broke what?

01:04:04.260 --> 01:04:04.640
Wait a minute.

01:04:08.960 --> 01:04:10.100
I just discovered something.

01:04:12.680 --> 01:04:14.020
Something I never realized.

01:04:14.020 --> 01:04:18.940
I know what woman means.

01:04:22.100 --> 01:04:25.580
She's not just the sort of a thing that you pursue and love and hold.

01:04:29.640 --> 01:04:29.980
Something...

01:04:30.000 --> 01:04:34.340
that leans over and whispers in your ear what you are,

01:04:36.700 --> 01:04:37.660
what you can do.

01:04:44.350 --> 01:04:46.310
Say, listen, let me tell you something.

01:04:47.520 --> 01:04:49.920
I'm sure it'll be a charming wedding whenever it happens.

01:04:50.250 --> 01:04:51.730
My dear, the boat sails in about an hour

01:04:51.730 --> 01:04:53.270
and I can't find Larry anywhere.

01:04:53.530 --> 01:04:54.230
Oh, he'll be here.

01:04:54.470 --> 01:04:54.950
Bye-bye.

01:04:55.230 --> 01:04:56.770
You know, I think I'm going to change these duds.

01:04:56.850 --> 01:04:58.790
We'll have to get married on the ship if I can find him.

01:04:59.080 --> 01:04:59.800
Why then, myself?

01:05:01.520 --> 01:05:03.960
Oh, well, stick around. We'll have a lot of fun anyway.

01:05:08.800 --> 01:05:11.260
I found him, boy, in conference down at the bank.

01:05:11.440 --> 01:05:12.940
And what he told him was nobody's business.

01:05:13.240 --> 01:05:14.760
He said he left a message with his secretary

01:05:14.760 --> 01:05:16.500
that he would be married at the town hall.

01:05:16.700 --> 01:05:18.260
He said the mayor was going to do it for him.

01:05:18.720 --> 01:05:20.820
I told him I wanted a wedding.

01:05:21.210 --> 01:05:23.090
Well, you win, boy. He's on his way up here now.

01:05:23.210 --> 01:05:24.370
He's changing his clothes right in the car.

01:05:25.760 --> 01:05:28.480
Oh, here he is. Oh, and I'm sorry.

01:05:30.570 --> 01:05:32.230
My dear, did you get my message?

01:05:32.550 --> 01:05:34.470
Oh, this is special. How do you do, sir?

01:05:34.830 --> 01:05:37.430
I think what I didn't tell those fellows at the bank isn't worth telling.

01:05:37.730 --> 01:05:38.750
Did you ever see this at your market?

01:05:38.950 --> 01:05:40.310
Watch copper open in the morning.

01:05:40.630 --> 01:05:41.590
I'm shooting at work.

01:05:42.810 --> 01:05:45.810
Larry, I'm watching Mr. Reverend Steele, Mr. Day.

01:05:45.890 --> 01:05:47.450
Well, how do you do, Mr. Steele? How are you?

01:05:47.590 --> 01:05:49.890
Steele? You've been going up right along, huh?

01:05:50.930 --> 01:05:51.550
That's funny.

01:05:52.050 --> 01:05:53.950
No, no, that's rude. I'm off with something.

01:05:54.590 --> 01:05:55.390
That's too bad.

01:05:55.790 --> 01:05:57.670
What do you do? Here, hold that together.

01:05:59.190 --> 01:05:59.870
Excuse me.

01:06:00.000 --> 01:06:02.220
Oh, now you're laughing at me.

01:06:02.400 --> 01:06:03.760
I always will.

01:06:04.200 --> 01:06:05.380
What do we do now, Vi?

01:06:09.280 --> 01:06:10.240
Steele. Steele.

01:06:10.780 --> 01:06:11.680
187 and a half.
